    "slug": "multiplication-table-using-for-else",
    "description": "Write a Python program that asks the user to enter a number and then the number of rows for the multiplication table. Use a for loop with an else clause to print the multiplication table. If the number of rows entered by the user is 10 or less, print the multiplication table up to the given rows. If the number of rows is more than 10, print the table only up to 10 rows and then print \"rows are limited to 10\" using the else clause. Each line should be printed in the format: number x i = result. The program must take both the number and the number of rows as input from the user.",
